{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794440400,"nonce":"ivLre4Umdgl8W9Cb5EdN0U31zdc=","message":"Progress, 2026-11-11: the additive core is written and tested (in the working tree, not committed).\n\nDone\n- `AnimationDescriptor`, `Curve` (`Linear`, `CubicBezier`, `Steps` with `StepJump`, `Power` with `PowerMode`, `Spring`), `evaluate`, `velocity`, `is_finished`, `retarget`, `descriptor::now_ms`, `lerp_color_premultiplied`. `Easing::to_curve`, `Spring::to_descriptor`, `AnimatedValue::descriptor`, `SchedulerHandle::get_spring`. Book page `animation/descriptors.md`, changelog, README untouched beyond the earlier fix.\n- The existing easings are cubic polynomials (`EaseIn` is t^3, not a CSS bezier) and powers, so `Curve::Power` is a fifth curve kind: it makes `to_curve` exact for all thirteen easings (checked to 1e-6 over a grid). The bezier solver is shared with `Easing`, so there is one definition.\n- Springs in closed form for under, critical and over damping, in f64 on the CPU. A spring's duration is its settling time: within a thousandth of its own scale, so unit-independent (tested). Compared with the RK4 `Spring` over six configs and three start conditions, up to where the integrator snaps to the target on its absolute 0.01 threshold.\n- One file of vectors: `tests/vectors/curves.txt`, 772 cases computed in float64 by `generate.py` from the maths alone. The CPU code agrees to 3e-7 of the distance moved, the shader (`sdf_russl/shared/curve.rs`, a russl library with a compute entry for the test) to 5.5e-7 on springs and under 2e-7 elsewhere, run on the M1 Pro. Acceptance asked for 1e-5.\n- Property tests: velocity is the slope of the value for every curve; retargeting a spring is continuous in value and velocity at any time to any target; retargeting a timed animation restarts from the current value over the full duration with no velocity (the CSS transition rule). No existing animation test changed: 70 pass in blinc_animation, 373 with blinc_gpu.\n\nNot done, on purpose\n- The read-back migration: `AnimatedValue::get`, `Spring::value`, `AnimatedTimeline::get`, `MotionBindings::get_*` and `MotionHandle::progress` evaluating a descriptor on demand, and with it the skip-ahead time semantics and the closed-form spring replacing RK4 in the existing `Spring`. That is the half that changes behaviour everywhere (scroll rebound, motion, every `use_spring`), so it wants its own change and its own tests, not a ride on this one. The umbrella's defaults (skip ahead on stall, closed-form springs) apply when it lands; CHANGELOG entry then.\n- The colour mix has no GPU test yet; it is first used in P5.\n\nNotes for P2\n- A shader takes `elapsed_ms` as an f32. If it is computed from an absolute f32 time it loses precision with uptime (about 1 ms at 3 hours), so P2 should send the frame time rebased to a recent origin, or send elapsed per row.\n- The shader's bezier solve is bisection (26 steps), not Newton, to keep it branch-free; it matched the float64 reference to 1.8e-7.","files":null}]}